course: dictionary
lesson: 5685
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Read the whole sentence first, then pick the meaning that fits. «The shop is in a good location near the station.» Here location means a place where something is.
explain: «The film was shot on location in the mountains.» On location means the film was made outdoors in a real place, not inside a studio. The words around the word are the clues.
explain: Location can also mean a position that a map, a GPS or a phone finds. In an emergency, «tell the operator your exact location» means say exactly where you are. Be careful about sharing your location online.
fact: A location is a place or position where something is or happens.
fact: «On location» means filmed outdoors in a real place, not in a studio.
fact: A GPS or phone can show your location as coordinates on a map.
fact: «Exact location» means the precise place, so always say it clearly in an emergency.
fact: Games often simplify places: «In the game each location has one owner, one sharp border and one population number.»
exercise: «The shop is in a good location near the station.» What does location mean here? | A kind of sweet | *A place where something is | A loud noise | A film made outdoors
exercise: «The film was shot on location in the mountains.» What does on location mean? | *Filmed outdoors in a real place | Lost somewhere in the mountains | Shown on a phone | Filmed inside a studio
exercise: In an emergency, why do you tell the operator your exact location? | So your phone battery lasts longer | So you can win a prize | *So help can find you quickly | So the operator can guess your age
test: «Your phone shows your location as coordinates on the map.» What does location tell you? | Which game you are playing | How fast you are walking | *Where you are on the map | What the weather will be
test: «In EU5 the far north has cold, harsh locations and the tropics hot ones.» What does this sentence suggest about real places? | Maps never show real places | *Climate depends a lot on distance from the equator | All places in the world have the same weather | Only the tropics have cold weather
exam: In «The far north has cold, harsh locations and the tropics hot ones», what does locations mean? | Rules | Maps | Lessons | *Places
